Day 26 – phpMyAdmin Dashboard (localhost)
 What is phpMyAdmin?

phpMyAdmin is a web-based interface used to manage MySQL databases.

Accessed via:
http://localhost/phpmyadmin
 
Dashboard Features Explored :
Database list & overview
Table structure view
SQL query execution tab
User accounts & privileges
Server information panel

Why phpMyAdmin Matters in Cybersecurity :
Misconfigured dashboards can expose databases
Attackers often target open phpMyAdmin panels
Understanding admin tools helps defend systems

 Security Best Practices Learned :
Restrict phpMyAdmin to localhost
Use strong database passwords
Apply least-privilege access
Never expose database dashboards publicly

 Key Takeaways

SQL is powerful.
phpMyAdmin makes it easy.
Security makes it safe.

Understanding how data is created, stored, and managed is essential for building secure web applications.
